# What belongs in git here is the source, not the output.
#
# A lesson is its .yaml. The .pptx beside it is produced by `python -m kit.build`
# and is reproducible from the .yaml plus the kit, so it is 130 MB of binary that
# would change on every rebuild and diff as noise. Rebuild instead of cloning it.
*/*/es/*.pptx
*/*/en/*.pptx

# The template and the instructor's original decks are sources, not output, so
# they stay tracked. Listed here so the rule above is not read as "no pptx".
!Programming_course_slide_template.pptx

# Reference material, not ours to redistribute. 628 MB of it, and two files are
# over GitHub's 100 MB hard limit, so a push carrying them is rejected outright.
# The Malik textbook additionally carries "may not be copied, scanned, or
# duplicated, in whole or in part" on its own cover.
*.pdf

# The MySQL course's inherited decks, 678 MB of them. They are the material the
# new course is being written to replace, the same role `Introducción al curso.pptx`
# plays for COM103, and they are reference rather than source. Keep them on disk,
# out of history.
mysql/PRESENTACIONES NUEVAS/
mysql/PRESENTACIONES ANTIGUAS/

# Working databases produced by the lessons that use sqlite.
*.db

# Preview contact sheets. They are throwaway, so they belong in a temp folder,
# but they land here by default and get forgotten.
/*-[0-9].png
/*-[0-9][0-9].png

__pycache__/
~$*
